{"toolCallId":"call_4514182914504c0a83e35cb57fe47417","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/224-deepseek-final2/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: producer/helper/policy] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: what owns the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: consumer/status/docs/tests] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: how it observes the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Components/functions] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: API endpoints/flows] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Tools] |\n| Manual | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/Library] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Internal/External] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Green/Yellow/Red] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n- **Trigger**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Draw the phase order in the fence, then fill the table with depends-on and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup to Implementation to Verification. Verification blocks close. WEAK: Phases depend on each other. -->\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n<!-- FILL: Give each phase an estimate and a total. Mark the total as an assumption. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup 10 minutes, implementation 30, verification 10. Total 50 minutes. WEAK: A few hours. -->\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger, the steps and the data reversal. Write `No` when no data changes. Delete the whole section when the packet ships no deployable service. GOOD: Trigger: default output changes. Steps: revert one commit, rerun the two commands. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n<!-- FILL: Draw the component order and fill the matrix with produces and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Script to test to close. WEAK: Components depend on each other. -->\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component A] | None | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | B, C |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component B] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component C] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component D] | B, C | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n<!-- FILL: Name the longest chain and its total. List what can run in parallel. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Implementation to verification, 40 minutes. Docs run in parallel. WEAK: The critical path is the main path. -->\n\n1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task A] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task C] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n<!-- FILL: Name three milestones with a command-checkable success criterion. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: M1: the branch exists. `rg -n quiet` prints it. WEAK: Milestones are tracked. -->\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Setup Complete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All dependencies ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Core Done] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Main features working] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Release Ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All tests pass] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n<!-- FILL: Write one ADR per decision. Name the context, the choice, the consequence and the rejected option. GOOD: ADR-001: a flag, because callers already pass flags. WEAK: We made a decision. -->\n\n### ADR-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Positive outcome 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Option B]: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one boolean global, one parser branch, one shared level-line helper and one output branch to recommend-level.sh, then prove the default report is byte-identical and the quiet path prints exactly one line.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2+ (the script runs under `set -euo pipefail`) |\n| **Framework** | None - standalone CLI script |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` plus shell assertions with `wc -l` and `diff` |\n\n### Overview\n\nChange one file, `recommend-level.sh`, in four small places: a `QUIET_OUTPUT` global, a `--quiet|-q` arm in the existing argument loop, a `_level_line()` helper shared by both text paths, and a dispatch branch that prefers JSON, then quiet, then the full report. Prove it by diffing the default report against baselines captured before the edit and by counting the quiet output's lines.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented in `spec.md` sections 2 and 3\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable: SC-001 through SC-004 each name a command\n- [ ] Dependencies identified: `bash` 3.2+, `wc`, `diff`, `node`\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met in `acceptance-criteria.md`\n- [ ] `bash -n .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` exits 0\n- [ ] The regression suite prints `passed=27 failed=0`\n- [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the flag name, the alias and the JSON precedence\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\n\nSingle script branch. No framework pattern applies: the change is one conditional output path inside an existing linear script.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]` loop, roughly lines 656-719): accepts `--quiet|-q` and sets `QUIET_OUTPUT=true`.\n- **Output dispatch** (roughly lines 770-774): selects `output_json`, the new quiet path, or `output_text`.\n- **`_level_line()` helper**: renders `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` once, so the report and the quiet path cannot drift apart.\n- **`output_text`** (roughly lines 508-558): keeps the full report; its level line now comes from the helper and stays byte-identical.\n- **`show_help`** (roughly lines 162-211) and the header OPTIONS block (roughly lines 16-27): document the new flag.\n\n### Data Flow\n\nargv enters the parser, which sets `LOC`, `FILES`, the risk flags, `RECOMMEND_PHASES`, `PHASE_THRESHOLD`, `JSON_OUTPUT` and now `QUIET_OUTPUT`. Scoring is unchanged. `determine_level` sets `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME`. Dispatch reads `JSON_OUTPUT` first, then `QUIET_OUTPUT`, then falls through to `output_text`; `--quiet` therefore changes only the final rendering step.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\nThe change is a feature, not a bug fix, but it touches an argument parser and a public stdout contract, so the surface inventory applies.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` argument parser | Owns which flags are accepted | update: add `--quiet` and `-q` | `rg -n -- '--quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the case arm |\n| `recommend-level.sh` output dispatch | Owns which renderer runs | update: JSON, then quiet, then text | `--quiet --json` still parses as JSON (AC-006) |\n| `output_text` | Owns the 17-line human report | update internals only: level line from `_level_line()` | Baseline diff is empty (AC-002) |\n| `output_json` | Owns the machine document | unchanged: not a consumer of `QUIET_OUTPUT` | JSON shape unchanged (AC-006) |\n| `show_help` and header OPTIONS | Own flag documentation | update: describe `--quiet` and `-q` | `--help` lists the flag (AC-004) |\n| `tests/test-phase-system.js` | Asserts phase and JSON fields through `--json` | not a consumer: run as regression | `passed=27 failed=0` (AC-008) |\n| Callers that parse the report | Read stdout by line position or label | not a consumer of quiet mode: default unchanged | Baseline diff is empty (AC-002, AC-003) |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` prints the report line and the helper.\n- Consumers of the changed flag: `rg -n -- '--quiet' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit` prints the script, this packet and any caller added later.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text, quiet, json), fixture (simple, complex), flag form (`--quiet`, `-q`), and input validity (valid, invalid). The verification tasks cover each axis at least once.\n- Algorithm invariant: not applicable - no path, redaction, resolver or security logic changes; scoring is untouched.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | stdout contract of the quiet path, the default path and the JSON path | `bash` assertions with `wc -l`, `diff`, and `node -e` for JSON parsing |\n| Integration | Phase recommendation and JSON fields consumed by the existing suite | `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` |\n| Manual | `--help` readability and flag discoverability | Terminal review of `--help` output |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| `bash` 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script cannot run; no fallback exists |\n| `wc`, `diff` | Internal | Green | Verification assertions cannot run; manual line counting stands in |\n| `node` 18+ | Internal | Green | SC-004 cannot run; the shell assertions still cover the new flag |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: the default report differs by any byte, or the JSON document changes shape.\n- **Procedure**: revert the commit that touched `recommend-level.sh`; the change is confined to one file, so no data or configuration cleanup follows.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────► Phase 2 (Core) ──────► Phase 3 (Verify)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core |\n| Core | Setup | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 30 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 15 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **55 minutes (assumption)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes) - N/A, the script writes no data\n- [ ] Feature flag configured - N/A, `--quiet` is itself an opt-in CLI flag\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set - N/A, the script runs on demand with no service\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the commit that touched `recommend-level.sh`.\n2. Rerun tasks T009 through T012, which cover both baselines, the quiet contract and the regression suite.\n3. Confirm the baseline diff is empty and the suite prints `passed=27 failed=0`.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A - no persistent state is written\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline fixtures | None | Two captured outputs in `scratch/` | Verification diffs |\n| `QUIET_OUTPUT` and parser arm | Baseline fixtures | A settable quiet mode | Output dispatch |\n| `_level_line` and `output_quiet` | Parser arm | The one-line renderer | Verification |\n| Verification tasks | Renderer and baselines | Acceptance evidence | Packet closure |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Capture baselines** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Implement the flag and the quiet renderer** - 30 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Verify both contracts** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: 55 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- T002 (capture baselines) and T003 (run the regression suite) can run simultaneously.\n- The header OPTIONS edit and the `show_help` edit touch different regions and can be made in either order.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baselines captured | `scratch/baseline-complex.txt` has 17 lines and `scratch/baseline-simple.txt` has 16 | After T002 |\n| M2 | Quiet mode implemented | `--quiet` prints one line and the default diff is empty | After T007 |\n| M3 | Verification green | T009 through T012 pass, suite prints `passed=27 failed=0` | After T012 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: A CLI flag, not an environment variable\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: Callers need a one-line mode. The script already takes every input as a CLI flag, and an environment variable would leak across invocations in the same shell.\n\n**Decision**: Add `--quiet` with `-q` as the short alias, matching the existing `--json, -j` and `--help, -h` pairs.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- The mode is explicit at each call site and composes with the other flags.\n- The parser grows by one case arm and the help text by one row.\n- The short alias adds a second spelling that must be tested, which AC-005 covers.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- `RECOMMEND_LEVEL_QUIET=1`: hidden state that survives across unrelated commands in the same shell, and it cannot be discovered from `--help`.\n- Always printing the compact form: breaks every caller that reads the report, so it is a breaking change rather than an option.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-002: `--json` wins when both flags are passed\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: `--quiet` defines a text shape and `--json` defines a document. Passing both leaves two plausible outputs and no defined quiet-JSON shape.\n\n**Decision**: Dispatch order is JSON, then quiet, then text. `--quiet --json` emits the JSON document unchanged.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- No half-format exists that a parser would reject.\n- A caller that wants one line uses the text form and omits `--json`.\n- AC-006 pins the behavior so it cannot flip silently.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Exit 1 on the combination: turns flag composition into an error and breaks callers that pass a shared flag set.\n- Trim the JSON to the level field: invents a third schema with no consumer.\n\n---\n\n### ADR-003: One helper renders the level line\n\n**Status**: Accepted\n\n**Context**: The quiet output must match the report's `Recommended Level:` line exactly. Two hand-written copies would drift on the first wording change.\n\n**Decision**: Add `_level_line()` and call it from `output_text` and `output_quiet`.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- The label and format have one source of truth, so a future change cannot update one path and miss the other.\n- `output_text` changes internally while its output stays byte-identical, which the baseline diff proves.\n- The helper adds one function call per invocation, below the timer's resolution.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- Duplicate the `echo` line in both functions: simplest diff, but guarantees future drift.\n- Have `output_quiet` call `output_text` and filter with `head -n 2`: adds a pipeline, depends on line position, and changes the process count.\n\n---\n\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":119,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":89}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/224-deepseek-final2/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
